Java is an object-oriented language, so every executable code resides inside a class. 
public class Solution defines the class that contains the program. The main method is the entry point 
recognized by the JVM. It is public so the JVM can access it, static so it can be invoked without 
creating an object, void because it doesn't return a value, main because the JVM looks for this 
exact method name, and String[] args allows command-line arguments to be passed to the program.